{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Round 3 results. (1) Haiku CV parity via prompt remediation: NOT achieved — two accuracy-tightening rules (state-not-provenance; trace-inferred-defects) kept Sonnet at 22/22 but Haiku only moved 86%→87% with complete-bugfix false-FAILing 3/3 epochs (over-literal evidence entailment — capability, not prompt). Zero false-accepts, but 2-3/11 pass-cases would false-block completed work. Keep Sonnet; patch preserved in worktree ../cv-prompt-remediation. (2) AC long tail: 48% of 3,054 historical ACs are hard-verification (30% absence/negative, 14% universal quantifiers); 93% of tickets have ≥1 hard AC — gold parity would understate production risk. (3) overlap-judge: no change needed — plan-review G6 correctly refuted my judge_one diagnosis (ticket 3939 closed not_a_bug); 48k rows were stale pre-fix checkouts; current failures are bounded $0.02 abstains. (4) Nova ceilings: change 1597 (ticket e800) LLM-Review +1, awaiting Verified. (5) Dependency sourcing for model limits: not available in pydantic-ai; genai-prices has context_window only; filed idea unrelaxed-trachyte-dipper."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786474792137526001,"uuid":"5ed00726-4998-4abe-b966-b8d08cb0b1ba"}